             324                     !
             325                     !>  Calculate the mass flux:
             326                     !!  \f[
             327                     !!  M = a_uw_u
             328                     !!  \f]
             329                     !!  where \f$a_u\f$ is the tunable parameter that represents the fractional area of updrafts (currently set to 0.08). Limit the computed mass flux to be less than \f$\frac{\Delta z}{\Delta t}\f$. This is different than what is done in Siebesma et al. (200
