             340                     !
             341                     !c!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
             342                     !  compute updraft property
             343                     !
             344                     !>  The updraft properties are calculated according to the entraining updraft equation
             345                     !!  \f[
             346                     !!  \frac{\partial \phi}{\partial z}=-\epsilon\left(\phi_u - \overline{\phi}\right)
             347                     !!  \f]
             348                     !!  where \f$\phi\f$ is \f$T\f$ or \f$q\f$. The equation is discretized according to
             349                     !!  \f[
             350                     !!  \frac{\phi_{u,k} - \phi_{u,k-1}}{\Delta z}=-\epsilon_{k-1}\left[\frac{1}{2}\left(\phi_{u,k} + \phi_{u,k-1}\right)-\frac{1}{2}\left(\overline{\phi}_k + \overline{\phi}_{k-1}\right)\right]
             351                     !!  \f]
             352                     !!  The exception is for the horizontal momentum components, which have been modified to account for the updraft-induced pressure gradient force, and use the following equation, following Han and Pan (2006) \cite han_and_pan_2006
             353                     !!  \f[
             354                     !!  \frac{\partial v}{\partial z} = -\epsilon\left(v_u - \overline{v}\right)+d_1\frac{\partial \overline{v}}{\partial z}
             355                     !!  \f]
             356                     !!  where \f$d_1=0.55\f$ is a tunable constant.
